1
00:00:04,168 --> 00:00:12,998
Package services and run a promotion — Growth ▸ Service Catalog — Price a service once, and it follows through booking, quotes and invoices.

2
00:00:18,361 --> 00:00:24,814
Growth ▸ Services is the catalogue: everything the clinic sells, priced once.

3
00:00:24,814 --> 00:00:34,851
That price is what booking, quotes and invoices all read — change it here and it changes everywhere.

4
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:44,014
Categories group them for the patient — chronic care, preventive, and so on.

5
00:00:44,014 --> 00:00:54,623
Packages bundle services at a set price, and show the saving explicitly — that is what makes them sell.

6
00:00:54,623 --> 00:01:06,957
Promotions carry a code, a discount and a window. They expire on their own, so nothing runs forever by accident.

7
00:01:06,957 --> 00:01:13,297
Statistics closes the loop: which services and packages actually get booked.

8
00:01:14,683 --> 00:01:26,723
What you just did

9
00:01:27,435 --> 00:01:36,435
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
